    "result_text": "All 3 acceptance tests pass and the build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented address normalization on owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1`.\n\n**New `normalizeAddress` helper** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:139`): trims and collapses whitespace, upper-cases, then expands abbreviations token-by-token (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). A `null`/blank value normalizes to `\"\"`.\n\n**Wired into `addOwner`** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:334`): the normalized address is written back onto the DTO as the very first step, *before* everything else. Because the DTO is the single source downstream, this makes the change satisfy every requirement without touching other methods:\n\n- **Required-field check** \u2014 `validateRequiredFields` reads `getAddress()`, now `\"\"` for an address that's blank after normalization, so it's rejected with a 400.\n- **Household duplicate detection** \u2014 `rejectDuplicateHousehold(..., getAddress())` compares the normalized form.\n- **Shared household id** \u2014 `householdId(..., getAddress())` derives from the normalized form.\n- **Store and return** \u2014 the mapper maps the normalized DTO address onto the persisted `Owner`, so it's stored and returned as `\"12 MAIN STREET\"` / `\"7 ELM AVENUE\"`.\n\nI kept the existing per-field `normalizeForHousehold` comparison intact \u2014 it's idempotent on already-normalized values, so existing owners (also stored normalized post-change) still compare consistently.\n\nFull test suite: **3 run, 0 failures, 0 errors \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.**",
